# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD 60fps, frame generation OFF, steady walking, -lock -etw, 2026-08-10; 1-member batches and a metronome grid - the stride-1 regime
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD 60fps, frame generation OFF, steady walking, -lock -etw, 2026-08-10; 1-member batches and a metronome grid - the stride-1 regime
# NO field lines: this capture ran in NEAREST mode (t:vsync), which logs no op= labels, so
# mktrace's field extraction read synth 0.0% as an artifact of the mode, not a measurement.
# The replay runs the composite decision regardless, so the bounds below gate the MODEL's
# behavior on this timeline (whole session: launch, menus, alt-tabs, one 2-min walk); there
# is no field fidelity check until an FG-off capture exists in blend mode.
#
# Pairing overrides, with the reason: with frame generation OFF a stalled/backgrounded game
# stops presenting and the flip grid pauses WITH it, so batches at stalls and regime
# transitions genuinely have no flips to pair against (whole-log placement measured 96.3%,
# p50 +114 us; the steady stretch pairs like the x2 walks). The x2 default of 98% encodes a
# grid that never pauses, which Smooth Motion provides and FG-off does not.
min_placed_pct 95
max_ahead_pct 2
max_worst_run 115
max_long_runs 2
max_synth_pct 14.3
min_reseeds 123
# Stage-6 gates, pinning the KNOWN alt-tab transition scramble so it can only improve
# deliberately. All 14 additions AND all 11 removals sit in one ~1 s cluster at t=53.4s
# where the game was backgrounded: the corrections that add them are issued at the END of
# the stationary 240 Hz desktop stretch and land at the desktop-to-game boundary. A grid-
# stationarity gate cannot fix this (the desktop interior is perfectly stationary; tried,
# parked on branch dejit-stationarity-gate) - the discriminator would have to be regime
# identity or boundary proximity, not window purity.
min_blends_removed 11
max_blends_added 14
arrivals 14467
